          "entradaId": "freeman-234",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The Hebrews, in common with all Oriental people, were very fond of riddles, and amused themselves with them, especially at ordinary meals and feasts. Even princes sometimes competed in their solution. The queen of Sheba tested Solomon’s wisdom with them. See 1 Kings 10:1 where th…",
        "traduccion": {
